       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-27 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by NDTV Sports, BBC Sport">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Abhishek Sharma's Rapid Ton Secures Series Win for India Against New Zealand</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#T20</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#New Zealand</span></div>
       <p>Abhishek Sharma powered India to a series-clinching six-wicket win against New Zealand in the third T20 International on Tuesday. Sharma unleashed a rapid 35-ball ton, scything through a hapless New Zealand attack, making even Vaibhav Sooryavanshi look like a bystander at times, according to NDTV Sports.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/abhishek-sharmas-rapid-ton-secures-series-win-for-india-agai.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>According to BBC Sport, Abhishek Sharma scored 113 runs from just 38 balls. His performance helped India successfully chase a target of 199 runs in only 13.2 overs, securing the victory. This dominant display ensured India's series triumph.</p><p>What to watch: Abhishek Sharma's continued performance in upcoming matches.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes information from two sources to provide a comprehensive summary of the match performance and series result.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/abhishek-sharmas-35-ball-ton-powers-india-to-series-win-in-new-zealand-12242634#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/cricket/articles/cvlyd05g6wypo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC Sport</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 2 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
