       <h1>Aptech, FTII Partner to Expand Film Education in India</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Film</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>Aptech and the Film and Television Institute of India (FTII) have joined forces to broaden film education opportunities across India, as reported by Telangana Today.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/aptech-ftii-partner-to-expand-film-education-in-india.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This collaboration aims to expand access to specialized training and courses within the film industry, making quality education more widely available throughout the country.</p><p>The partnership signifies a strategic move to address the growing demand for skilled professionals in various aspects of filmmaking.</p><p>What to watch: The rollout and accessibility of new film education programs.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately summarizes the provided information. It is concise and covers all essential points from the source.</p>
