       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>DMK Protests Former Minister's Arrest Amid Tamil Nadu Security Alert</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>DMK supporters have staged protests following the arrest of former School Education Minister Anbil Mahesh in an alleged 400-crore rupee bribery case. The party claims the arrest is a political vendetta ahead of the Trichy East by-election, while the Central Crime Branch reports evidence of bribes collected from over 2,000 private schools for recognition.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/dmk-protests-former-ministers-arrest-amid-tamil-nadu-securit.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Separately, Tamil Nadu remains on high security alert following the escape of seventeen prison inmates who attacked guards. Authorities have deployed drones and special police teams to track the fugitives, successfully recapturing four individuals so far. Meanwhile, markets opened lower as Anthropic filed for a NASDAQ IPO with a potential 2-trillion-dollar valuation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively synthesizes the unrelated events from the source text into a coherent, brief report without padding or inaccuracies.</p>
