     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>ECI Files Supreme Court Affidavit Rejecting Unilateral Decision Allegations</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Election Commission of India (ECI) has submitted a formal affidavit to the Supreme Court to address claims regarding the Special Intensive Revision (SIR) of electoral rolls. The Commission explicitly rejected allegations that Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar acted unilaterally during the process. In its filing, the ECI maintained that all three official orders related to the SIR exercise were passed unanimously by the commission's three members. This legal response serves as a defense against public accusations of procedural impropriety within the electoral body.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/eci-files-supreme-court-affidavit-rejecting-unilateral-decis.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the ECI affidavit regarding the SIR exercise and the rejection of unilateral decision-making claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/videos/breaking-news/eci-defends-cec-gyanesh-kumar-in-supreme-court-over-sir-controversy-delhi-protest-news18-10399122.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
