       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>FATHI Demands Immediate Release of Educational Dues</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Federation of Associations of Higher Educational Institutions in Telangana (FATHI) has urged the state government to release long-pending fee reimbursement and scholarship funds. The association reports that unpaid dues from previous years and the 2026–27 cycle are hindering college operations, including staff salary payments and infrastructure maintenance.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/fathi-demands-immediate-release-of-educational-dues.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The delays have also caused issues for students, with some graduates unable to access academic records. FATHI requested that the government clear at least 50% of arrears, deposit reimbursements for graduates directly into institutional accounts, and settle all outstanding dues for eligible minority students.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately conveys the demands and grievances of FATHI as stated in the text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/fathi-urges-govt-for-release-of-rtf-dues/article71632383.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
