     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Jan Suraaj Party Official Found Dead After Disappearing from Train</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Devpalik Gupta, the 31-year-old digital communications manager for Prashant Kishor’s Jan Suraaj Party, has been found dead near railway tracks in Ranchi. Gupta went missing on Monday afternoon while traveling on the Ranchi-Patna Janshatabdi Express.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/jan-suraaj-party-official-found-dead-after-disappearing-from.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Police recovered his body in bushes near Jarwadih after his colleagues reported him missing. Preliminary investigations suggest Gupta may have fallen from the moving train and suffered a head injury, though the circumstances remain under investigation. The party has called for an impartial probe into the death of the aide, who had worked with Kishor since 2022.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively captures the essential details of the incident and the party's stance without unnecessary padding.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/prashant-kishor-media-manager-missing-train-found-dead-conspiracy-3026176-2026-10-27?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
