       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Jharkhand Authorities Search Hospital After Viral Video Shows Dog With Newborn</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Authorities in Jharkhand have launched an investigation at Medinirai Medical College and Hospital after a viral video surfaced showing a stray dog carrying what appeared to be a newborn baby. Officials conducted a thorough search of the hospital campus, including the post-mortem house and surrounding shrubbery, but have not yet located the infant or the dog.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/jharkhand-authorities-search-hospital-after-viral-video-show.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Deputy Commissioner Dilip Pratap Singh Sekhawat has ordered a coordinated review of CCTV footage and interviews with local staff and residents. The administration aims to verify the video's authenticity, determine if any negligence occurred, and establish accountability for the incident.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and captures the essential details, including the location and the administration's investigative steps.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/jharkhand-hospital-viral-video-search-newborn-carried-by-stray-dog-medinirai-medical-college-and-hospital-in-palamu-ptag-3026382-2026-10-27?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
