     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Variety · 2026-10-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Joy Behar Returns to The View Following Dislocated Shoulder</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Comedian Joy Behar returned to the ABC talk show The View on Tuesday after an absence of nearly one month. The 84-year-old had not appeared on the program since September 30 following a backstage fall that resulted in a dislocated shoulder.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/joy-behar-returns-to-the-view-following-dislocated-shoulder.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Behar received a standing ovation from the studio audience upon her return. Describing the severity of her injury, the host noted that the pain she experienced was worse than childbirth. She remains a regular fixture on the daytime panel.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise and accurately reflects the provided source material regarding Behar's return and injury.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/joy-behar-the-view-return-dislocated-shoulder-1236932092/" rel="noopener">Variety</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
