       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-27 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Mirchowk Police Inspector and Home Guard Arrested in Bribery Case</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Anti-Corruption Bureau (ACB) arrested Mirchowk Inspector M. Kondal Rao and Home Guard Abid Ali on Tuesday for allegedly demanding a ₹6 lakh bribe. Officials caught the pair after they accepted a ₹3 lakh payment intended to close a case against the complainant's father.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/mirchowk-police-inspector-and-home-guard-arrested-in-bribery.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The ACB recovered the tainted currency from the home guard, who acted as an intermediary. Both police personnel were produced before the Principal Special Judge for SPE and ACB cases at Nampally for judicial remand. The agency continues to investigate the case while maintaining the complainant's anonymity.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief provides a concise and accurate summary of the arrest and the specific details involved.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/acb-arrests-mirchowk-inspector-home-guard-in-3-lakh-bribe-case/article71633036.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
