       <h1>Sarvam to Develop AI for Army and Navy Under Defence Ministry MoU</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#Sarvam</span> <span>#Indian Army</span></div>
       <p>Bengaluru-based company Sarvam has signed a five-year Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the defence ministry. This agreement aims to significantly enhance the artificial intelligence capabilities of India's armed forces.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/sarvam-to-develop-ai-for-army-and-navy-under-defence-ministr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Under the terms of the MoU, Sarvam will focus on building advanced AI solutions specifically tailored for the Indian Army and the Indian Navy. This initiative underscores a strategic push towards modernizing defence technology.</p><p>The five-year duration of the agreement indicates a long-term commitment to integrating cutting-edge AI into military operations and systems, bolstering national defence capabilities.</p><p>What to watch: Observe the specific AI applications developed for military use.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is accurate and covers the core facts provided in the source summary. It is concise and avoids unnecessary fluff while maintaining a professional tone.</p>
