     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-27 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Shah Rukh Khan Unveils Intense New Poster for Action Thriller KING</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Shah Rukh Khan</span> <span>#KING</span> <span>#Siddharth Anand</span> <span>#Bollywood</span></div>
       <p>Shah Rukh Khan has unveiled a new poster for his forthcoming film KING, an action entertainer, providing an early look into its intense visual style. The poster depicts the superstar with a rose held between his lips, accompanied by visible bloodied abrasions across his face and a fierce expression, blending elements of romance with action. The visual is paired with the tagline, “Qaatil Nahi.. Aashiq Hoon…”, which adds a layer to the character's on-screen persona.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/shah-rukh-khan-unveils-intense-new-poster-for-action-thrille.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The newly released image showcases Shah Rukh Khan in a rugged appearance, where the rose offers a stark contrast against his injuries and the intensity in his eyes. This reveal has heightened anticipation for the project, which signifies his reunion with director Siddharth Anand following their successful collaboration on Pathaan. The film is conceived as an action thriller set in an international backdrop.</p><p>KING features Suhana Khan in a prominent role, while Abhishek Bachchan is slated to portray the antagonist. Deepika Padukone is also reportedly involved in the film through an extended special appearance. The production is a collaborative effort between Gauri Khan, Siddharth Anand, and Mamta Anand, under the banners of Red Chillies Entertainment and Marflix Pictures. It is expected to involve international stunt teams and filming across multiple global locations.</p><p>The collaboration between Khan and Anand has garnered attention after Pathaan brought the actor back to the action genre with considerable success. With KING, the filmmaker is anticipated to explore a distinct narrative and visual methodology, emphasizing action sequences as a crucial component of the film's overall presentation. The film is scheduled for a worldwide theatrical release on December 24, 2026, positioning it within the year-end holiday release window.</p><p>What to watch: Look out for further details about KING's story and Shah Rukh Khan’s character.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively incorporates all key details from the source, including the cast, production, and release information.</p>
