     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-27 · editor 7/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Sub-Inspector and Student Killed in Separate Road Accidents</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Two separate road accidents in Tiruvannamalai and Ranipet districts resulted in the deaths of a police sub-inspector and a school student on Tuesday. R. Parthiban, 50, died after an unidentified vehicle struck his motorcycle while he was returning from temple security duty near Vandavasi.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/sub-inspector-and-student-killed-in-separate-road-accidents.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In Ranipet, 15-year-old R. Monish was killed when a van hit the two-wheeler he was riding with his sister near Walajah town. Monish died at a government hospital in Sholinghur following the collision. Police have launched investigations into both fatal incidents.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft contains a small error regarding the hospital location for the student, citing Sholinghur while the source specifies the hospital type and location differently.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/two-killed-in-separate-road-incidents/article71631434.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
