      <a href="/feed.xml" title="RSS">RSS</a>
      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/world">world</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-27 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>US Midterm Elections Set for November 3</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Americans head to the polls on November 3 for midterm elections that will determine control of Congress, governorships, and thousands of state offices. Democrats need a net gain of three House seats and four Senate seats to secure majorities, while Republicans aim to maintain their current legislative standing.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-27/us-midterm-elections-set-for-november-3.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Campaign spending is expected to reach approximately $12 billion, surpassing previous records. Recent polls show Democrats leading on the generic congressional ballot, though presidential approval ratings for Donald Trump remain low across several surveys. Voters have expressed significant concern regarding the impact of current administration policies on the economy.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the electoral context and financial figures provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/us-midterms-470-seats-12-billion-and-one-absent-president-ws-l-10400372.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
